{{Culture of Balisca}}
{{Life in Balisca}}
'''Baliscan society''', often labelled a "{{W|Post-work society|leisure society"}}, embodies the [[Baliscan art|artistic]], [[Baliscan cuisine|culinary]], [[Baliscan literature|literary]], [[Baliscan humor|humoristic]], [[Music of Balisca|musical]], [[Politics of Balisca|political]] and social elements that are representative of Balisca. Throughout Balisca's early history, its culture had been influenced by a plethora of cultures, including [[Indigenous peoples in Balisca|indigenous peoples]], [[W:Andalusians|Andalusians]], Levantines, [[W:Arab-Berbers|Arab-Berbers]], [[W:Catalans|Catalans]], [[W:Occitans|Occitans]] and [[W:Sephardic Jews|Sephardic Jews]]. Over time, elements of the cultures of migrants to Balisca have been incorporated into the Baliscan {{W|cultural mosaic}}. Certain segments of Balisca population have, to varying extents, been influenced by other {{W|Latin American culture}}s due to geographic and linguistic proximity, and high media penetration.

Balisca is often characterized as being "{{W|cosmopolitanism|cosmopolitan}} and {{W|permissive society|permissive}}" society. Balisca's [[Politics of Balisca|confederal government]] has often been described as been the passive of multicultural ideology because of its primary emphasis on the concepts of [[W:self-determination|self-determination]],[[W:Solidarity|solidarity]] and [[W:Egalitarian community|egalitarianism]], especially regarding [[Immigration to Balisca|immigration]]. Baliscan culture draws from its broad range of constituent nationalities, and policies that promote a {{W|just society}} have been implemented at the confederal level. Confederal policies include the denunciation of [[W:Capital punishment|capital punishment]]; [[Social protection in Balisca|strong efforts]] to eliminate [[Balisca#Income, wealth, and poverty|poverty]]; an emphasis on [[W:Cultural mosaic|cultural diversity]]; denunciation of [[W:Postgenderism|gender]] and [[W:Racism|racial theory]], the recognition of gender and [[LGBT rights in Balisca|sexual]] diversity, [[Abortion in Balisca|pregnancy terminations]], [[Euthanasia in Balisca|euthanasia]] and [[Drug policy of Balisca|recreational drugs]] — are social indicators of the country's [[politics of Balisca|political]] and [[Baliscan values|cultural values]]. 

